WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.703
-Hi, everybody.
Welcome to another edition

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:05.871
of "Tonight Show:
At Home Edition."

00:00:05.871 --> 00:00:09.275
And it's very rainy
and cold here,

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:12.111
but I am braving the storm
while my wife

00:00:12.111 --> 00:00:16.516
and dog and kids are safe
and cozy on the inside.

00:00:16.516 --> 00:00:18.551
And I hope that you are
safe and cozy

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:20.820
on the inside of your home.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:23.723
It's a great day
to stay at home.

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:25.525
We have a fun show tonight.

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:28.327
Blake Shelton is here,
country music legend.

00:00:28.327 --> 00:00:29.895
Why was I doing that --

00:00:29.895 --> 00:00:31.965
What was I proving by being --
nothing.

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:33.766
I was proving nothing
by being outside.

00:00:33.766 --> 00:00:36.602
Anyway, I'm inside now,

00:00:36.602 --> 00:00:38.938
and I hope you guys are inside
as well, safe.

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:40.806
Blake Shelton
is on the show tonight.

00:00:40.806 --> 00:00:42.675
He's doing a song
with Gwen Stefani

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:45.477
to close our show called
"Nobody but You"

00:00:45.477 --> 00:00:47.713
off of his album,
"Fully Loaded."

00:00:47.713 --> 00:00:50.883
His charity tonight
is MusiCares.

00:00:50.883 --> 00:00:54.153
They're doing something for
people in the music industry

00:00:54.153 --> 00:00:55.855
affected by COVID-19.

00:00:55.855 --> 00:00:58.257
It's a great charity.
Thank you for being here, Blake.

00:00:58.257 --> 00:01:00.259
Also from "Saturday Night Live,"
you know him, you love him,

00:01:00.259 --> 00:01:01.961
he's also in
"Trolls World Tour,"

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:03.929
Kenan Thompson is here tonight.

00:01:03.929 --> 00:01:05.798
[ Clapping ]
Ah! We love Kenan,

00:01:05.798 --> 00:01:11.871
and his charity is
nokidhungry.org.

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:15.408
And then later we'll be
playing a game,

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:18.111
an online game called
"Quiplash," which I love.

00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:20.780
And the makers of that game,
Jackbox,

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:24.850
said that they will match
up to $25,000

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:27.487
in donations to
redcross.org.

00:01:27.487 --> 00:01:29.522
So thank you guys for that,
and please donate

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:32.058
when the time comes
if you're watching on YouTube.

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:33.759
I'll be playing with
some fun people.

00:01:33.759 --> 00:01:36.196
Alright, let's start the show
with a fun monologue.

00:01:36.196 --> 00:01:38.798
Here we go.
♪♪

00:01:38.798 --> 00:01:41.067
Welcome to "The Tonight Show:
At Home Edition."

00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:43.536
Well, guys, the weather here
has been crazy.

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:46.272
All day there's been
thunderstorms with wind gusts

00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:48.541
of over 70 miles per hour.

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:50.343
I can tell my wife is getting
tired of me.

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:52.144
Today she told me
to take a selfie stick

00:01:52.144 --> 00:01:53.746
and go film on the roof.

00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:58.684
I almost got a chair squeak
out of that one.

00:01:58.684 --> 00:02:00.953
-[ Chuckles ]

00:02:00.953 --> 00:02:04.223
-That's right, the wind was
over 70 miles per hour.

00:02:04.223 --> 00:02:06.192
The only fun part of the day
was gathering the family

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:08.060
in front of and open window
and re-enacting

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:10.063
Beyoncé at Coachella.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.635
Let's get to some news.

00:02:15.635 --> 00:02:18.838
Earlier today, Bernie Sanders
endorsed Joe Biden for President

00:02:18.838 --> 00:02:20.739
in a joint live stream.

00:02:20.739 --> 00:02:23.676
Yep, and like most streams
involving those two,

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:25.144
they stood there
for a few minutes

00:02:25.144 --> 00:02:26.913
waiting for it to happen.

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:31.584
Well, guys, the CDC now says
that the coronavirus

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:34.254
can be spread
through your shoes.

00:02:34.254 --> 00:02:35.989
Which means everyone's
about to become that

00:02:35.989 --> 00:02:37.756
annoying dinner party
host who goes,

00:02:37.756 --> 00:02:40.159
"Do you mind
taking off your shoes?

00:02:40.159 --> 00:02:42.694
Thank you.
We just got our carpet cleaned.

00:02:42.694 --> 00:02:45.565
And so, you know, just --

00:02:45.565 --> 00:02:47.433
or you can leave
them on if you want.

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:50.436
We'll just -- we'll feed you
through the window."

00:02:52.705 --> 00:02:54.907
Alright. I always had that
one neighbor growing up

00:02:54.907 --> 00:02:57.076
that I had to like take
my shoes off and I go,

00:02:57.076 --> 00:03:00.213
"Really? You think your house
is that nice?

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:02.682
Okay."

00:03:02.682 --> 00:03:04.583
Okay.

00:03:04.583 --> 00:03:05.985
Some TV news --
over the weekend

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:10.890
ESPN aired a seven-hour National
Spelling Bee marathon

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:15.227
and then a tournament of NBA
players playing horse.

00:03:15.227 --> 00:03:17.663
Then afterwards, everyone turned
to the Weather Channel

00:03:17.663 --> 00:03:19.799
just to feel something again.

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:24.070
A new "Bachelor" spin-off
called "Listen to Your Heart"

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:25.872
premiered tonight,
where 20 singles try

00:03:25.872 --> 00:03:28.674
to connect romantically by
making music together.

00:03:28.674 --> 00:03:31.110
So if you think it's bad when a
guy whips out an acoustic guitar

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:33.979
at a party, imagine
the entire party

00:03:33.979 --> 00:03:36.382
is filled with that guy.

00:03:38.050 --> 00:03:41.453
And finally, a 93-year-old
Pennsylvania woman went viral

00:03:41.453 --> 00:03:43.889
after putting a sign
in her window that read,

00:03:43.889 --> 00:03:45.825
"I need more beer."

00:03:45.825 --> 00:03:47.726
[ Chuckles ] Yeah,
it was funny until

00:03:47.726 --> 00:03:49.629
everyone realized it was
a 33-year-old woman

00:03:49.629 --> 00:03:52.765
who's having
a rough quarantine.

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:54.867
It got even crazier when she
turned the sign around

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:57.036
and it said, "And shrooms."

00:03:57.036 --> 00:03:59.905
You guys, that is our monologue
right there.

00:03:59.905 --> 00:04:03.142
I wanted to check in on
my friend and our announcer,

00:04:03.142 --> 00:04:05.578
Steve Higgins, who is at home
safely with his family.

00:04:05.578 --> 00:04:07.847
Steve Higgins,
how you doing, bud?

00:04:07.847 --> 00:04:09.315
-How's it going, Jimmy?

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:11.117
-It's so good to see you, man.
I miss you.

00:04:11.117 --> 00:04:14.153
Oh, Zoom background.
-Fantastic, huh?

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:16.789
-Yeah. That's a good one.
I don't have that one.

00:04:16.789 --> 00:04:19.291
-I upgraded to Pro.
It's fantastic.

00:04:19.291 --> 00:04:20.893
-What is that one called?

00:04:20.893 --> 00:04:23.663
-It's called
Tropical Paradise.

00:04:23.663 --> 00:04:26.732
-I have like Space
and San Francisco.

00:04:26.732 --> 00:04:28.334
That's all I have.

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:30.436
-Oh, dude, you got to
upgrade to Pro.

00:04:30.436 --> 00:04:32.271
Check out this one,
this one is fantastic.

00:04:32.271 --> 00:04:33.572
-What is this called?

00:04:33.572 --> 00:04:36.642
-It's called
Man Looking at Waterfall.

00:04:36.642 --> 00:04:37.876
Look at that.
-Mm.

00:04:37.876 --> 00:04:39.678
-Majesty of the waterfall.

00:04:39.678 --> 00:04:43.616
-Yeah, why not just show
the waterfall? I mean...

00:04:43.616 --> 00:04:45.484
-You can kind of see it
in his eyes

00:04:45.484 --> 00:04:48.020
if you look real close.
-Can you?

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:50.122
-Well, look, he's pointing
at it, see?

00:04:50.122 --> 00:04:53.092
-No. What else do you got?

00:04:53.092 --> 00:04:57.696
-Oh, this is my favorite one.
Check this one out.

00:04:57.696 --> 00:05:00.032
-Is that a bag of dog food?
-Yeah, it's like I'm hanging out

00:05:00.032 --> 00:05:01.534
in front of a big bag
of dog food.

00:05:01.534 --> 00:05:03.769
Check it out, it's like
I'm almost there.

00:05:03.769 --> 00:05:06.672
-Oh, yeah.
-I'm gonna grab that dog food.

00:05:06.672 --> 00:05:08.240
-Is there any other ones?

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:11.744
-Oh, you're gonna love this one.
Boom.

00:05:11.744 --> 00:05:14.814
-Ew, what's that?
-Mystery celebrity armpit.

00:05:14.814 --> 00:05:16.549
Whose is it? We don't know.

00:05:16.549 --> 00:05:19.351
-Mystery celebrity armpit?
-Yeah.

00:05:19.351 --> 00:05:21.587
-Ew. [ Laughs ]

00:05:21.587 --> 00:05:24.790
I wouldn't be able to guess
any celebrity armpit.

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:27.693
-No, that's why it's so great,
'cause it's a mystery.

00:05:27.693 --> 00:05:29.228
-Hey, I should get going, dude.
This was --

00:05:29.228 --> 00:05:30.863
-You know what?
-What?

00:05:30.863 --> 00:05:32.731
I got to go, though.
-Mystery solved,

00:05:32.731 --> 00:05:34.700
it's my armpit.

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:36.868
-[ Laughs ]
You got me, dude.

00:05:36.868 --> 00:05:38.537
Very good.
That's great, buddy.

00:05:38.537 --> 00:05:40.539
Nice to see you again.
Take care, okay?

00:05:40.539 --> 00:05:44.377
-Wait, how are Franny
and Winnie?

00:05:44.377 --> 00:05:46.712
-They're great.
They're so cute, I know --

00:05:46.712 --> 00:05:49.114
Oh -- There's your kid,
your family's there too.

00:05:49.114 --> 00:05:50.983
-Hi.
-They love you. They --

00:05:50.983 --> 00:05:53.252
[ Laughs ]
-Yeah!

00:05:53.252 --> 00:05:54.921
-So much fun.

00:05:54.921 --> 00:05:57.089
[ Talking over each other ]

00:05:57.089 --> 00:06:00.993
[ Laughter ]

00:06:00.993 --> 00:06:02.328
-Oh, my God.

00:06:02.328 --> 00:06:04.630
[ Laughter ]

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:05.831
-Yeah!

00:06:05.831 --> 00:06:08.334
[ Laughter continues ]

00:06:08.334 --> 00:06:09.701
-All right.

00:06:09.701 --> 00:06:11.871
Well, all right, I'll see you --
you guys are nuts.

00:06:11.871 --> 00:06:13.039
-Bye, Jimmy.

00:06:13.039 --> 00:06:16.041
-We'll see ya, Jimmy.
I'm bleeding pretty bad.

00:06:16.041 --> 00:06:18.711
-All right, guys.
We'll check in with you later.

00:06:18.711 --> 00:06:20.313
-Oh, my God.
Who turned the lights out?

